@page "/intermediate/050"

<h1>Exercise 050 - JsInteropReturnValue</h1>

@* Prerendering is disabled on the component itself, not the page: the solution
   calls JS interop from OnInitializedAsync, which throws during a static-prerender
   pass because no circuit/JS runtime exists yet. Putting @rendermode on the page
   instead would statically-render nothing at all - the whole body, heading and
   inline <script> included, would only exist once the interactive circuit patches
   it into the DOM, and Blazor does not execute a <script> inserted that way. Kept
   on the tag so the page (heading, script) stays statically rendered and only this
   component's own render is deferred to the circuit. *@
<Ex050_JsInteropReturnValue @rendermode="@(new InteractiveServerRenderMode(prerender: false))" />

<script>
    window.app = window.app || {};
    window.app.load = function () {
        return "loaded from host";
    };
</script>
